// S-959 (W5-11 U10d2/t2, §2.5, §6.4, §6.5, §18.1): the candidate of the E0020 of `@ derive(PartialEq)` (with a space after the
// `@`) takes the attribute out, with the space, and writes the name at the head of the declaration (`: PartialEq`), and
// nothing is left behind (`clean`, S-253). The main position is the attribute, from the `@`. A file with one unit, so that
// `clean` looks at the whole file.

@ derive(PartialEq) pub struct S {   //~ E0020
  id: U32,
}
